the target language is: lps.

% Late Delivery and Penalty (Accord Project). Deadlines and elapsed time.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/CLOUT_workshop/deliveryDelay.pl
%
% "In case of delayed delivery the Seller shall pay to the Buyer for every day
%  of delay a penalty amounting to 20% of the total value of the Equipment
%  whose delivery has been delayed. The total amount of penalty shall not
%  exceed 50% of that value. If the delay is more than four days, the Buyer is
%  entitled to terminate this Contract."
%
% The real-time plumbing -- simulatedRealTimeBeginning/1, the end_of_day poll
% and real_date_add/3 -- is external Prolog and lives in the companion file
% delivery_delay.lps (docs/le_lps_surface.md §7).

the maximum time is 32.

the prolog events are:
    the day ends on *a date*; known as end_of_day.

the events are:
    *an order* is delivered; known as deliver.

the actions are:
    *an order* is terminated; known as terminate_order.

the fluents are:
    *an order* has been delivered; known as delivered.
    the penalty on *an order* is *an amount*; known as penalty.
    *an order* is under force majeure; known as force_majeure.
    *an order* has been cancelled; known as terminated.

the templates are:
    the seller of *an order* is *a person*.
    the buyer of *an order* is *a person*.
    the latest delivery date of *an order* is *a date*.
    the total value of *an order* is *an amount*.
    the penalty percentage of *an order* is *a rate*.
    the penalty cap of *an order* is *a rate*.
    *a first date* is *a number* days after *a second date*; known as real_date_add.

the knowledge base delivery delay includes:

initially the penalty on mydelivery is 0.0.

the seller of mydelivery is bob.
the buyer of mydelivery is alex.
the latest delivery date of mydelivery is 2018-04-01.
the total value of mydelivery is 100.
the penalty percentage of mydelivery is 0.20.
the penalty cap of mydelivery is 0.50.

when the day ends on a second date
    and the latest delivery date of an order is a first date
    and it is not the case that the order has been delivered
    and the second date is a delay days after the first date
    and it is not the case that the order is under force majeure
    and it is not the case that the order has been cancelled
    and the total value of the order is a value
    and the penalty percentage of the order is a rate
    and the penalty cap of the order is a cap rate
    and a new penalty is the rate * the value * (the delay + 1)
    and a cap is the cap rate * the value
    and the new penalty is less than or equal to the cap
then the penalty on the order that is an old penalty becomes the new penalty.

when an order is delivered
then the order has been delivered.

if the day ends on a second date to a first time
    and the latest delivery date of an order is a first date
    and it is not the case that the order has been delivered at the first time
    and the second date is a delay days after the first date
    and the delay > 4
then the order is terminated from the first time to a second time.

when an order is terminated
then the order has been cancelled.

scenario one is:
    mydelivery is delivered from 12 to 13.
